Z||000000||fotofrank||04-24-2000||09:24 AM||||Gents, The positive lead from my battery is shorted to ground. Battery will not hold a charge. Arcs and sparks when connecting the leads to the battery.The car is a '84 2.5L. Any sugestions? I'm quesing the starter or altinator,possible the ignition switch.What connector can I disconnect at the firewall to aliminate everything outside of the engin compartment?||||reg||8
Z||000001||Oreif||04-24-2000||09:29 AM||||You can rule out the ignition switch. The wire has a "fuseable link" so if the ignition switch shorts it will open. Have you changed starter or alt lately? The other thing to check would be the wires, The ones that go near any exhaust pipes. There is a block behind the battery that can overheat and cause a short too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fotofrank||04-24-2000||05:53 PM||||Did not change starter or alternator. Those are my first ques along with melted wires.||||reg||9
